{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe close-reason and force plumbing is computed independently on each surface: the \"reason persists only on a REASON_REQUIRED class without force\" rule lives at `src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:584`, `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py:318`, and `src/rebar/_commands/txn.py:357-362`; the `\"(no reason given)\"` placeholder at `transition.py:388`, `claim.py:38`, `_lib_writes.py:412`; one datum travels as `force_reason` → `force_close` → `force_close_reason` across three files. The CLI refuses an inadmissible reason while the library silently discards it, and MCP `transition_ticket` (`src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:224-232`) does not expose `reason` at all — the strict-xfail row in `tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py:34-35,193` (bug `scratchy-leprous-galago`). Bug `defiant-orthoclase-buck` was the datum accepted under one name and never read.\n\n## Approach\nAdd `src/rebar/_commands/transition_request.py` with a frozen `TransitionRequest(ticket_id, current, target, close_class, reason, force, caused_by, ref)` exposing `force_note`, `close_reason`, and `reason_refusal()`. All three surfaces construct it; `txn.transition_core` and `close_ticket` read the properties. MCP `transition_ticket` gains `reason` by constructing the same object, which flips the strict-xfail to a pass and forces its removal. Guard: the placeholder literal and the REASON_REQUIRED admission test appear only in `transition_request.py`.\n\n\n## Guard construction\nFollow the guard-test construction rule in the parent epic `airborne-wellloved-kingfisher`: owner module exempt, match the constituent conjunction or AST shape named in Approach (or the definition count where no distinctive atom exists), `# <construct>-ok: <reason>` escape marker, and behaviour pinned only by the named existing tests.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_commands/transition_request.py` (new), `src/rebar/_commands/transition.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/claim.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/txn.py`, `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py`, `tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py`, `tests/unit/commands/test_transition_request.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: each surface closing a REASON_REQUIRED class with a reason persists it. Edge: a reason on a non-reason class is refused identically on CLI, lib, and MCP (the parity oracle row). Pinning: `tests/interfaces/test_write_parity_oracle.py`, `tests/unit/test_transition_close.py`, `tests/unit/test_administrative_close_dispositions.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py` pass unchanged except the removed xfail marker.\n\n\n## The `(no reason given)` oracle, corrected (review remediation)\nThe earlier AC-2 demanded `grep -rn \"no reason given\" src/rebar` return exactly ONE file. That\ncannot pass, and should not: the literal occurs **12 times across 4 files**, and only **3 are\ncode** —\n- code: `_lib_writes.py:247`, `_lib_writes.py:412`, `_commands/transition.py:396`\n- prose: `_deprecations.py:100` (a comment), `_lib_writes.py:235,238,278,385`,\n  `transition.py:65,264,343,390` (docstrings and help text that legitimately NAME the value\n  they document).\n\nA guard that forbade documentation from naming the placeholder would be deleted the first time\nsomeone wrote a docstring. So the construct is the **production of the value**, not the mention\nof it: the placeholder becomes a single named constant on the value object\n(`TransitionRequest.NO_REASON_GIVEN`), and the guard asserts the string LITERAL is assigned in\nexactly one place under `src/rebar`, with a `# force-reason-ok: <why>` escape. Docstrings and\ncomments are out of the scan by construction (the scan looks for the literal in an assignment or\nreturn expression, not anywhere in the line), so prose stays free.\n\n`src/rebar/_deprecations.py` is NOT added to Scope: its occurrence is a comment, and under the\ncorrected oracle it needs no change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The `write_parity_contract.py` reason row passes on all three adapters with its strict-xfail removed; checked by `pytest tests/interfaces/test_write_parity_oracle.py`.\n- [ ] `grep -rn \"no reason given\" src/rebar` returns one file; checked by the grep and the guard test.\n- [ ] Persisted `force_close_reason` and `close_reason` events are byte-identical to today for the pinning suites; checked by those suites passing unchanged."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787365674207792001,"uuid":"9ea2e463-5c51-4e3e-b3a0-a70139b9012c"}